{"help": "https://data.humdata.org/api/3/action/help_show?name=package_search", "success": true, "result": {"count": 2, "facets": {}, "expanded": {}, "results": [{"archived": false, "caveats": "\u2022\tData are based on rapid assessments and may not capture all hazards or long-term risks due to time and resource constraints.\r\n\u2022\tThe information is preliminary and intended for initial emergency response; detailed site-specific investigations should follow.\r\n\u2022\tSome data may be incomplete or rely on remote or secondary sources, especially where access was limited.\r\n\u2022\tHazard identification and risk prioritization reflect the situation during the assessment; conditions may change with follow-up monitoring.\r\n\u2022\tFEAT tables focus on acute chemical and environmental risks and may not address all chronic or indirect impacts.\r\n\u2022\tMethodology relies on standardized assumptions; local context and expert input are recommended for interpretation.\r\n\u2022\tUse caution when applying findings to areas outside the original geographic or temporal scope.", "creator_user_id": "4ee49cf6-a5aa-45ec-8391-f0b45a94b0f5", "data_update_frequency": "-2", "dataset_date": "[2021-11-19T00:00:00 TO 2022-02-25T23:59:59]", "dataset_preview": "first_resource", "dataset_source": "UNEP/OCHA Joint Environment Unit", "has_geodata": false, "has_showcases": false, "id": "19865ab7-1554-4633-a423-f9d16d586bbc", "is_requestdata_type": false, "isopen": true, "last_modified": "2025-11-13T09:49:01.809822", "license_id": "cc-by", "license_title": "Creative Commons Attribution International (CC BY)", "license_url": "http://www.opendefinition.org/licenses/cc-by", "maintainer": "4ee49cf6-a5aa-45ec-8391-f0b45a94b0f5", "metadata_created": "2025-11-13T09:48:32.896383", "metadata_modified": "2025-11-13T11:51:38.521400", "methodology": "Registry", "name": "flash-environmental-assessment-tool-feat-tables-12-countries", "notes": "This tables presents results from the Flash Environmental Assessment Tool assessments conducted in 12 countries in Latin America in Q4 2021 and Q1 2022.\r\n\r\nThe FEAT helps to identify potential hazards posed by hazardous operations. The FEAT is used at the onset of hazardous operations or disasters, by international humanitarian responders that may be unfamiliar with the affected area.\r\n\r\nThe FEAT was initially developed based on lessons stemming from the 2004 Indian Ocean Earthquake and Tsunami, with the aim to provide a standardized, scientific assessment methodology to prioritize the impacts of chemical accidents following large scale, sudden onset natural disasters.\r\n\r\nThe outcome of the FEAT is the identification of impact zones (areas most at risk from hazardous chemical releases). These zones highlight locations where urgent response actions are needed to protect human health and the environment.\r\n\r\n[More information on the FEAT Tool](https://www.unocha.org/publications/report/world/flash-environmental-assessment-tool-feat-20-pocket-guide)", "num_resources": 10, "num_tags": 3, "organization": {"id": "d1beab07-c452-4877-8c6d-c7ab3d086ecd", "name": "unep-ocha-jeu", "title": "UNEP/OCHA Joint Environment Unit", "type": "organization", "description": "The United Nations Environment Programme (UNEP) and United Nations Office for the Coordination of Humanitarian Affairs (OCHA) Joint Environment Unit (JEU) responds to environmental dimensions of emergencies by coordinating international efforts and mobilizing partners to support countries that have requested assistance. In doing so, the JEU offers a wide range of services to holistically address the links between environment and emergencies.", "image_url": "", "created": "2025-11-03T09:35:07.253838", "is_organization": true, "approval_status": "approved", "state": "active"}, "owner_org": "d1beab07-c452-4877-8c6d-c7ab3d086ecd", "package_creator": "diegoreyes11", "pageviews_last_14_days": 0, "private": false, "qa_completed": false, "solr_additions": "{\"countr